+declaration/module changes and additions/deletions re-resolve the changed files and their
+recorded lookup consumers. Positive and negative name lookups and module-path probes are
+tracked, so new overloads, previously missing declarations and re-export changes can heal
+without visiting every source fragment. Module-configuration edits still re-resolve all
+disk fragments without reparsing unrelated source files. Unchanged saves skip parsing
+and do not advance the generation.
+
+Reverse dependencies and a deduplicated work queue are stored in the same staged graph,
+not a project-sized Java map. Per-file evidence is capped at 4,096 uncached lookup
+observations / 1 MiB estimated tracking records. A file exceeding either bound is marked
+for conservative re-resolution on any declaration/module change. Missing legacy evidence
+forces a full rebuild rather than trusting an incomplete dependency inventory.
 
